[dvystrcil/gpu-batch] n8n-lane-a job fails with FileNotFoundError on /work/TEMPLATE/status.json.1  (model=qwen3-coder-next:latest, 29s, lane=claude)
## Why
The `n8n-lane-a` Job in the `gpu-batch` namespace is failing with a `FileNotFoundError` when trying to write status to `/work/TEMPLATE/status.json.1`. This breaks the batch lane execution flow.

## What we know
- The failing pod is `gpu-batch/n8n-lane-a-20261107t074604-k88z7`, exit code 1.
- Error traceback shows `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/work/TEMPLATE/status.json.1'` in `runner.py`, line 85 (`tmp.write_text(...)`).
- The pod `gpu-batch/n8n-lane-a-20261107t074604-r2-4j4fg` completed successfully, indicating earlier steps work but the status-write step fails.
- The `gpu-batch-work` PVC is mounted at `/work` (per architecture docs and `base/work-volume.yaml`).
- The path `/work/TEMPLATE/` must exist for `status.json.1` to be written; if it doesn’t, `pathlib.write_text()` raises `FileNotFoundError`.
- **unverified**: Whether `/work/TEMPLATE/` is created by prior containers or should be pre-created by the Job spec.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] **AC1.** The `n8n-lane-a` Job completes without `FileNotFoundError` when writing status.
- [ ] **AC2.** The `/work/TEMPLATE/` directory exists before the status write step runs (either by prior container or Job init).
- [ ] **AC3.** A test run of `gpu-batch-submit.py --lane a` succeeds end-to-end.

## Lane
claude — the failure is in the runner logic and volume setup; unclear whether the directory should be created by the Job template or by a prior container, and requires inspecting the full Job manifest and runner.py behavior.

